                  "fill": "#1c1d21",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "The SN2 reaction is a concerted nucleophilic substitution. A single-step concerted process where the nucleophile attacks from the back side, leading to configuration inversion at the chiral carbon center.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.4,
                  "fontFamily": "Lora",
                  "fontSize": 14,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
